# OKF Knowledge Catalogue — agent onboarding

The catalogue is a read-mostly, LLM-facing knowledge store, separate from any
Obsidian vault it may be opened in. It holds thematic *bundles*; a bundle is a
folder of Markdown *concepts*, each with YAML frontmatter carrying a non-empty
`type`. A concept-id is its path below the bundle, minus `.md`. The store is a
plain git repo — ordinary file tools and git apply.

## Retrieve — by command, not by blind grep

Progressive disclosure: widen only when the cheaper step left the question open.

  1. find "<query>"             ranked search across all bundles; narrow it with
                                --where "type = Runbook and path ~ <bundle>/"
  2. index [<bundle>]           what bundles and directories exist
  3. toc <bundle>[/<concept>]   headings before bodies — the cheapest way to
                                decide whether a page is worth reading. A bare
                                <bundle> or <bundle>/<subdir> resolves to its
                                index.md, so the names listed below are the
                                argument, verbatim.
  4. read <bundle>/<concept>    the page itself. `read --section "<heading>"`
                                prints one section; `read --follow N` adds the
                                pages it links to (`--inbound`: also those
                                linking to it)
  5. refs / wikilinks           follow the graph out of a page

## Write — through the ce-okf skill, never by hand

Concepts are not hand-authored: `ce-okf` routes a source to a bundle, applies
frontmatter and re-indexes. `index.md` listings are marker-managed and
generated — never edit between the `<!-- okf:... -->` markers. A commit is
allowed only once `check` reports zero violations.

commands by purpose:
  navigation:
    ctx              context bundles: curated, ordered reading lists per topic (`ctx` lists them, `ctx <slug>` shows one)
    index            catalogue TOC (bundle names + one-line descriptions), or one bundle's index.md
    info             print catalogue schema docs (TYPES.md + PROPERTIES.md)
    list             list the complete, unranked set of concepts a required --where expression selects
    prime            one-shot agent onboarding: usage guide, command directory, catalogue state and bundle TOC
    read             print one concept page
    recent           list the most recently created concepts, newest first
    sync-export      print a canonical block's payload for materialisation elsewhere
    toc              print a concept's headings (default: h2 only)
    visualize        write a viz.html concept graph for a bundle (embeds every concept body; needs network for cytoscape/marked)
  search:
    build-index      (re)build the FTS5 lexical search index at <root>/.fts/fts.sqlite (local only, no network)
    build-semantic-index fill <root>/.tagvec/tag_vectors.sqlite's concept_emb table for every concept still missing a voyage-3-large embedding (NETWORK, requires VOYAGE_API_KEY)
    find             hybrid ranked search: lexical FTS5/BM25 arm plus semantic arm
    refs             list inbound and outbound markdown links of a file
  tags:
    merge-tags       merge/rename one or more tags into a target tag across concept frontmatter
    normalize-tags   convert inline `tags: [...]` fields to YAML block-list form (local convention)
    remove-tags      remove one or more tags from concept frontmatter (no merge target)
    tags             list all tags with usage counts, or fuzzy-search candidate tags
  maintenance:
    archive          move a concept into _archive/<bundle>/, or back with --restore (dry-run default)
    check            conformance scan: §9 hard rules + local invariants
    fix-crosslinks   rewrite links to catalogue-root-absolute form (/bundle/subdir/concept.md)
    fix-xml-tags     wrap `<tag>`/`<tag>.<tag2>` placeholders in inline code
    install          register okf, its agent skill, MCP server and shell completion with this machine's agents and shells (dry-run default; needs no catalogue)
    migrate          migrate frontmatter to OKF 0.2: `timestamp` to `generated` (git), `status` per D37 (dry-run default)
    registry         reformat registry entries of TAGS.md or TYPES.md (table or block form); prose stays
    reindex          (re)generate marker-bounded index listings: index.md one level, index-map.md the whole subtree
    rename           move a concept + rewrite every inbound/outbound link + reindex (dry-run default)
    rewrite-path     literal path-string rewrite across text files
    sync-insert      materialise a canonical block inside a consumer concept (dry-run default)
    sync-status      drift report for every materialised canon block
    sync-update      re-materialise outdated consumer blocks from their canon owner (dry-run default)
    verify           record that a concept was checked against its sources
    wikilinks        report Obsidian wikilinks ([[…]]) and whether each resolves to a concept

## find — the entry point

usage: okf find [-h] [--include-topics] [--limit LIMIT] [--where EXPR] [--breakdown]
                [--expand-tags] [--json]
                query

Each result line's headline number is `rank: N` — its 1-based position in
the delivered list, the one scale comparable across a mixed-arm result
because it IS the list order (D12: handover, never blend by score). The
arm's own raw value is not in that column; pass `--breakdown` to see it,
per hit: `score: a/b` for a lexical hit (a/100 is the FTS5/BM25 arm,
relative to this run's own top hit; a/(6 * n) is the substring fallback
used when no FTS index is available, over n query terms), `score: cosine
X.XX` for a semantic hit — its own scale, never the same column as a
lexical a/b. `provenance:` names the arm that produced the line.
Degradations are announced on stderr.

Full flag semantics: `find --help`.

